        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "perf(home): batch publisher hydration (#3067 / #2925)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- What changed: This PR proposes one bounded public publisher-summary query for the ten pinned home publishers and requests it once as the section approaches the viewport.\n- Why: The home page currently hydrates ten full publisher profiles serially. The proposed query reads only normalized, unique handles, preserves publisher and linked-user visibility, and leaves incomplete or unavailable publishers on the static fallback cards.\n\n## Linked Issue\n\n- Closes #3067\n- Related #2925\n\n## Screenshots\n\n- [x] Real fallback and hydrated ClawHub captures are embedded in a PR comment.\n\n## Behavioural Proof\n\nOn the real home page with a local Convex fixture, the publisher section rendered ten static fallback cards with zero summary requests above the fold. Scrolling 700 px issued exactly one `publishers:getHomePublisherSummaries` request containing the ten pinned handles; repeated scrolling issued no additional requests. The one-result fixture response was 339 bytes of JSON and 617 encoded transfer bytes, and the hydrated card changed from `Explore creator` to `Explore 1 item`.\n\n- [x] Behavioural proof included\n\n## Security / Trust Impact\n\n- [x] No security/trust impact. The proposed summary query reuses publisher and linked-user visibility rules and omits incomplete denormalized counters.\n\n## Data / Deploy Impact\n\n- [x] No data/deploy impact. No schema, migration, backfill, or production deployment is required.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `bun run ci:static`\n- [x] Focused tests: `bun run test -- convex/publishers.test.ts src/__tests__/home-popular-publishers-section.test.tsx`\n- [x] `bun run ci:unit`\n- [x] `bun run ci:types-build`\n- [x] `bunx convex codegen`\n- [x] `git diff --check`\n",
